## 🔥 Common Pitfalls & Anti-Patterns

### ❌ DON'T: Duplicate Package Code in Apps

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: apps/editor/src/utils/history.ts
export class HistoryManager { /* ... */ }

// This belongs in packages/editor-utils!
```

### ❌ DON'T: Import with Relative Paths Between Packages

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
import { Vec3 } from '../../../packages/core/src/math/Vec3';

// ✅ GOOD
import { Vec3 } from '@engine/core';
```

### ❌ DON'T: Create Circular Dependencies

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
// packages/world/src/Scene.ts imports from gfx-webgpu
// packages/gfx-webgpu/src/Renderer.ts imports from world
```

### ❌ DON'T: Allocate in Hot Paths

```typescript
// ❌ BAD (called 60 times per second)
update(dt: number) {
  const velocity = new Vec3(); // Allocates every frame!
  velocity.set(this.vx, this.vy, this.vz);
}

// ✅ GOOD
private tempVelocity = new Vec3(); // Reuse

update(dt: number) {
  this.tempVelocity.set(this.vx, this.vy, this.vz);
}
```

### ❌ DON'T: Forget Cleanup

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
test('animation plays', () => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => { /* ... */ }, 100);
  // Test finishes, interval keeps running!
});

// ✅ GOOD
test('animation plays', () => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => { /* ... */ }, 100);
  
  // Cleanup
  afterEach(() => {
    clearInterval(interval);
  });
});
```

